   "source": [
    "# \uD83C\uDFD8️ HUD-VASH Voucher Utilization & Source of Income (SOI) Anti-Discrimination Laws\n",
    "**Course:** Massive Data Fundamentals (Georgetown University — McCourt School of Public Policy)  \n",
    "**Instructor:** Peter Nicewicz  \n",
    "**Objective:** Evaluate whether state and municipal \"Source of Income\" (SOI) anti-discrimination laws causally improve the utilization rate of HUD-VASH housing vouchers for homeless veterans.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "### \uD83D\uDCDA The Policy Problem\n",
    "Through the **HUD-VA Supportive Housing (HUD-VASH)** program, the federal government allocates rental assistance vouchers to Public Housing Authorities (PHAs) to house veterans experiencing homelessness. However, a voucher is only a subsidy on paper: veterans must still find private-market landlords willing to accept it. In tight rental markets, landlords frequently reject voucher holders outright—a practice that is completely legal under federal law unless prohibited by a state or local **Source of Income (SOI)** anti-discrimination statute.\n",
    "\n",
    "### \uD83C\uDF93 Pedagogical Architecture: Why Databricks & Apache Spark for Public Policy?\n",
    "| Platform Component | Why We Use It in Public Policy Data Science |\n",
    "| :--- | :--- |\n",
    "| **Apache Spark (Distributed Compute)** | Administrative microdata (e.g., Census ACS PUMS, IRS tax panels, CMS claims) scales to tens of millions of rows. Single-node `pandas` hits Out-Of-Memory (OOM) bottlenecks on joins; Spark partitions data across worker nodes in parallel. |\n",
    "| **Lazy Evaluation & Catalyst Optimizer** | Spark separates *Transformations* (`read`, `filter`, `join`) from *Actions* (`saveAsTable`, `count`, `display`). It waits until an Action is called to compile an optimized physical execution plan (DAG), pushing filters down to storage before shuffling data across the network. |\n",
    "| **Delta Lake & Unity Catalog** | Policy research requires strict reproducibility and auditability. Saving analytical tables in **Delta format** provides ACID transactions, schema enforcement, and **Time Travel** (`VERSION AS OF`), allowing agencies or peer reviewers to reproduce the exact dataset used in a congressional testimony or published paper. |"
   ]
  },
