   "source": [
    "## \uD83D\uDCBE Phase 3: Load into the Lakehouse (Save as Gold Delta Table & Verify Audit Trail)\n",
    "\n",
    "> **\uD83C\uDF93 Teaching Moment — Why Save as a Delta Table Instead of Keeping DataFrames in Memory?**  \n",
    "> 1. **Materializing the DAG:** Writing `df_joined` to `hud_vash_analytical_base` executes the physical Spark plan and persists the cleaned data in columnar Apache Parquet format wrapped with a `_delta_log` transaction log.  \n",
    "> 2. **Auditability & Reproducibility (Federal OIG & Academic Peer Review):** In federal oversight (e.g., an Office of Inspector General audit or GAO review) or academic peer review, you must prove exactly what the data looked like when a model was estimated. Delta Lake's `DESCRIBE HISTORY` and `VERSION AS OF` allow instant time-travel queries without duplicating storage.  \n",
    "> 3. **Decoupled Compute:** Once saved as a Unity Catalog table, policy analysts can query `hud_vash_analytical_base` directly in Databricks SQL Dashboards without re-running the Python ETL pipeline."
   ]
  },
