      "========================================================================================\n\uD83D\uDCCA ECONOMETRIC COMPARISON: NAIVE BIVARIATE vs. CONTROLLED MULTIVARIATE OLS (HC3 ROBUST SE)\n========================================================================================\n• Naive OLS Effect of SOI Law (No Controls):      +4.20 pp (SE: 0.31, p = 1.1952e-41)\n• Controlled OLS Effect of SOI Law (Full Model):  +6.03 pp (SE: 0.22, p = 2.7816e-163)\n  -> Omitted Variable Bias Corrected:             +1.83 percentage points!\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n                            OLS Regression Results                            \n==============================================================================\nDep. Variable:       utilization_rate   R-squared:                       0.516\nModel:                            OLS   Adj. R-squared:                  0.515\nMethod:                 Least Squares   F-statistic:                     530.8\nDate:                Sat, 31 Oct 2026   Prob (F-statistic):               0.00\nTime:                        14:02:03   Log-Likelihood:                -6493.8\nNo. Observations:                2180   AIC:                         1.300e+04\nDf Residuals:                    2174   BIC:                         1.303e+04\nDf Model:                           5                                         \nCovariance Type:                  HC3                                         \n================================================================================\n                   coef    std err          z      P>|z|      [0.025      0.975]\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nIntercept       93.2223      0.768    121.385      0.000      91.717      94.728\nhas_soi_law      6.0260      0.221     27.231      0.000       5.592       6.460\nmedian_rent     -0.0106      0.000    -24.625      0.000      -0.011      -0.010\npoverty_rate    -0.1988      0.022     -8.918      0.000      -0.243      -0.155\nvacancy_rate     0.3390      0.012     29.166      0.000       0.316       0.362\nveteran_pct      0.0097      0.041      0.237      0.813      -0.071       0.090\n==============================================================================\nOmnibus:                        5.279   Durbin-Watson:                   2.035\nProb(Omnibus):                  0.071   Jarque-Bera (JB):                5.285\nSkew:                          -0.106   Prob(JB):                       0.0712\nKurtosis:                       2.884   Cond. No.                     7.57e+03\n==============================================================================\n\nNotes:\n[1] Standard Errors are heteroscedasticity robust (HC3)\n[2] The condition number is large, 7.57e+03. This might indicate that there are\nstrong multicollinearity or other numerical problems.\n\n========================================================================================\n\uD83E\uDD16 DISTRIBUTED PYSPARK MLlib: RANDOM FOREST PREDICTIVE RISK MODEL\n========================================================================================\n• Out-of-Sample Test RMSE: 4.71 percentage points\n• Out-of-Sample Test R²:   0.498\n• Distributed Feature Importances (Predictive Triage Drivers):\n    - vacancy_rate      : 0.430\n    - median_rent       : 0.230\n    - has_soi_law       : 0.207\n    - veteran_pct       : 0.074\n    - poverty_rate      : 0.059\n"
