   "source": [
    "## \uD83C\uDFA8 Phase 6: Audience-Tailored Policy Visualizations (Academic, Federal Oversight, & Legislative)\n",
    "\n",
    "> **\uD83C\uDF93 Teaching Moment — Why One Chart Does Not Fit All Audiences:**  \n",
    "> A data scientist who shows a regression partial-residual plot to a Senate staffer will lose the room in 10 seconds; conversely, showing a simple bar chart without confidence intervals or covariate controls at an academic econometrics seminar will get torn apart during peer review. Below, we generate a **3-Panel Multi-Audience Executive Figure** tailored to the three core public policy forums:\n",
    "> \n",
    "> 1. **Panel A — The Academic / Econometric Forum (McCourt / NBER / APPAM):**  \n",
